<description>
Recolor each small monochromatic foreground object green while leaving larger objects unchanged.

Input structure
- The dominant color is the background.
- The foreground is split into monochromatic 4-connected objects of several colors.
- Green is absent from the input and is the output marker color.

Rule
- Find every non-background same-color 4-connected object.
- If an object's area is one or two pixels, recolor all of its pixels green.
- Keep objects with area at least three unchanged.

Key insight
The selected pixels are the complete small color-components, independent of their color or position.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects on the background",
  "transform": "recolor each object of area one or two pixels green; preserve objects of area at least three and the background"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 3-9 rows x 3-8 cols
  background: black (0); dominates the grid [observed]
  foreground_colors: 3-4 non-green, non-black colors (green is absent from input)
  components: monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects
    small: area 1-2 pixels; 2-15 per grid; at least 1 required
    large: area 3-5 pixels; 1-7 per grid; bbox typically 1-3 rows x 1-4 cols
    total: 3-19 components
  color_overlap: same color may appear in both small and large components
  foreground_density: 0.45-0.67 of grid cells are non-background
  transform: recolor every small component (area <= 2) to green (3); leave large components and background unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct forward construction
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims (rows 3-9, cols 3-8) and 3-4 fg colors from non-green, non-black palette.
    2. Place 1-7 large components (area 3-5, 4-connected, monochromatic) on the black grid without overlap.
    3. Scatter 2-15 small components (area 1-2 each, monochromatic) in remaining empty cells; ensure no small component merges with another same-color foreground pixel (would create a larger connected component).
    4. Verify fg density is 0.40-0.70 and green is absent.
    5. Output is a copy with all small-component pixels recolored to green.
  merge_avoidance: when placing a small component pixel, check that no 4-neighbor has the same color (unless it is the other pixel of the same 2-pixel small component). This prevents accidental merging into a larger component.
```
